←: 40 - ~~**Snake portrait board far too small — shape-aware fit ([REDACTED_SECRET])**~~ Done. The flat `{top,bottom,left,right}` clearance model shrank Snake's board to ~67% of the container width, wasting the entire center gap between the D-pad's two narrow corner columns. Fixed with `Render.fitBoardShapeAware` (Snake portrait only): binary-searches the largest hexagonal board whose actual cells clear each real chrome rectangle (stats + the two `.snake-pad-cluster` columns individually) by the gap, letting the board be nearly full width with its tapering lower flanks sliding into the center gap — the SVG box's own empty corners are what overlap the columns, never a real cell. Cell positions are predicted through the exact `getFitView`→viewBox mapping snake.js applies downstream, so the prediction can't drift from what renders. Gravity/Blast keep the flat path (their boards genuinely are bounded by full-width chrome bands). Not yet extended to Snake landscape (its D-pad is full-height left/right co …[3503 chars elided]… g would need to rotate correspondingly to stay intuitive — a real design question, not just a rendering tweak. Related to #28 (device rotation as viewing angle). Not yet started. 44 - **Compose: extend/overdub recording**: two related gaps raised after chord entry landed. (1) Resuming a stopped recording currently restarts its clock at 0 (`recordStartTime` resets unconditionally in `startRecording`), so there's no way to "add the next 4 measures" onto an existing take without it overlapping the start. (2) Overdub/layering: re-recording separate takes anchored to the *same* start point, then merging them into one note list, is a real mouse-compatible path to chords (one voice per pass, merged after) since a mouse can never produce simultaneous input the way multitouch can. Needs its own design pass (is layering a UI toggle? does merge just flatten to one list on save, or keep layers distinguishable? how does Undo interact with a layer boundary?) before implementation -- not yet started.


