Yes — in music theory, "note name + octave" (like "[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]" or "[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]") is just called a **pitch** (as distinct from "pitch class," which is the letter alone, octave-agnostic — "C" as opposed to "[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]"). The convention of writing it as letter+octave-number is **Scientific Pitch Notation** (SPN), which is exactly what this UI already does.

So "pitch" is the term already sitting there unused — e.g. "pitch row" or "pitch label" for the aligned strip, rather than inventing something new.


