←: 978 ### [REDACTED_SECRET]: a cell always sounds its own pitch — the founding invariant 979 980 This is the founding invariant of the whole project. A cell at `(p, q)` sounds **exactly** 981 `Tonnetz.getFrequency(getMidi(p, q))` — its own pitch — *everywhere, always, in every mode*. What 982 may vary per context (mode, cell state, event) is timbre/instrument, volume, and attack/decay/ 983 duration. What may **never** vary is the **pitch**. The Tonnetz position *is* the pitch; that 984 mapping is inviolable. There is no per-mode exception: the restricted modes (Snake/Blast/Gravity) 985 aren't a different rule, they're simply *restricted* to fewer cells, each of which still sounds its 986 own pitch. 987 988 Consequences that follow directly: 989 - **No octave-folding.** The synth must never shift a note into a "comfortable" register to make 990 it audible — that plays a *different pitch*. It commands the note's true frequency across the 991 whole range of human hearing and beyond; whether a given de …[866 chars elided]… ars pitch (see Life #13). 1002 1003 **Test:** `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` — "[REDACTED_SECRET]: the synth sounds each note at its own true 1004 getFrequency(midi), never octave-shifted" sweeps a range of MIDI values (including the extremes the 1005 old fold used to relocate) and asserts the synth commands exactly `getFrequency(midi)` for each. 1006 The lattice-reach half is covered in `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` ("Tonnetz draws cells up to the top of 1007 human hearing"). 1008 1009 **Accepted trade-off:** Gravity's board tuning (`35 − 3p + 4q`) spans ~130 semitones (MIDI 23–153), 1010 so with the fold gone its top rows are genuinely ultrasonic and go unheard, and its low end is 1011 comparatively high. On review ([REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]) the honest-pitch result sounded good enough in play that 1012 a retune wasn't worth it — the top was judged fine and, at most, the bottom could drop an octave 1013 someday. So this is a known, accepted characteristic, not an open task. This invariant is what 1014 surfaced it. 1015


