### 2026-08-17T16:37:50.744Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Found and fixed it — thank you for catching that. The regression was a genuine off-by-one in the code I wrote earlier this session: the condition that grows the drilled segment required the just-played note's index to be *strictly greater* than `endIndex`, but on the very first note (segment `[0,0]`), playing note 0 correctly gives `userIndex-1 === endIndex` (0 === 0), not greater — so the segment never grew, and the game just kept replaying note 0 forever. Fixed in `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` (`handleUserInputNote`), and I found that the regression test I'd written earlier had actually been written to match that same broken behavior (`[0,1,2,3]` instead of the correct `[1,2,3,4]`), so it passed without catching the bug. Verified live end-to-end: playing note 0 now correctly extends to note 1 and prompts you to continue.


