Done. Summary:

- **Vendored `[REDACTED_SECRET]`** (MIT-licensed) into `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`, same LibreJS-wrapped pattern as VexFlow — verbatim upstream UMD build, wrapper comment for `docs/librejs-compliance.md`, license text in `[REDACTED_SECRET]`, documented in `js/vendor/README.md`.
- **`Life.parseYaml`** is now a one-line call to `jsyaml.load`; the ~150-line hand-rolled recursive-descent parser (block/flow collections, comment stripping, scalar coercion) is gone.
- **`LifeMode.toYaml`** now builds a plain object and calls `jsyaml.dump` instead of hand-assembling text lines.
- Hit one real snag along the way: `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`'s Node `vm` test harness runs `life.js` and `[REDACTED_SECRET].js` in different V8 realms, so [REDACTED_SECRET]'s own "is this a plain object" check (which requires exact same-realm `Object.prototype`) rejected ordinary `{}` literals. Fixed by building the object graph with `Object.create(null)` instead — `null` has no realm, so it satisfies the check everywhere, including the real browser where this makes zero difference.
- Verified all 15 bundled `life/*.yaml` files still parse correctly, plus the full test suite (215 desktop, 18 Life-specific, unit tests) is green.


