### 2026-08-18T18:58:40.467Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

The background Tablet Chrome test run is still in progress — I'll get notified when it completes rather than poll further.

**Summary of the marker/measure-advance investigation**: I traced the reported "half-measure" advance to a real ordering bug — `updateDifficultyUI()` (which repositions the start marker) was being called *before* the measure-advance logic that actually updates `startIndex`, so on the exact note that triggers a 3-clean-pass advance, the marker rendered one note late. Fixed by moving that call after the advance block, with a regression test using a 2-note measure (where the lag is unambiguously "half a measure"). Both of your replay files predate this fix (`[REDACTED_SECRET]`), so they're consistent with this being the cause.

Separately, finishing the top-bar redesign surfaced a few real layout bugs I've now fixed: Compose's board briefly using a stale (pre-shrink) zoom fit on mode entry, its taller control panel needing internal scroll instead of squeezing the board to nothing, and the controls/Timeline not actually spanning full width when stacked on a narrow phone. All covered by new tests, all green on Desktop Chrome, Mobile Chrome, and (pending) Tablet Chrome.


