Both commits are in. Summary of this final push:

1. **[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]** — a single `#notation-bar` with controls on the left (capped under half width) and the Timeline filling the rest, replacing the two-tier layout you flagged as wrong. Stacks (thin controls, then Timeline, then Tonnetz) on narrow widths instead of a separate mobile mechanism — consistent everywhere, as asked, and the old melody-only mobile dock/drawer split is gone.
2. **Notation now fills available width** — `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` stretches per-measure spacing to use the space it's actually given instead of always rendering at a fixed content-driven size, which was the real cause of the wide empty space you saw.
3. **Two layout bugs found and fixed along the way**: Compose's board was fitting against a stale (pre-shrink) size on mode entry, and Compose's taller control panel needed its own scroll budget so it couldn't squeeze the board to nothing.
4. **The "half-measure" marker bug** — a real ordering bug: the marker-repositioning call ran before the code that actually advances `startIndex`, so it rendered one note late. Fixed and covered by a test that reproduces exactly what you described.

Full suite green on Desktop/Mobile/Tablet Chrome aside from three pre-existing, independently-confirmed flakes unrelated to any of this.


