Good question — the Timeline *component* (rendering, marker DOM, drag mechanics in `[REDACTED_SECRET]`) is genuinely shared. But each mode owns its *own* `startIndex`/`endIndex` state and decides independently what to initialize them to before handing them to `timeline.refresh()`. Melody's default lives in `resetGame()` (already fixed earlier this session, `[0, 1]`); Compose's lives in `refreshStaff()`'s own separate "first note(s) just appeared" branch — that's the one that had the `[0, 0]` bug. Same shared rendering, two independent initialization sites, only one was wrong.

