### 2026-08-19T03:10:50.140Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

That would avoid duplicate folder scans/fetches between the two dropdowns, but it needs `[REDACTED_SECRET]` itself restructured — right now `setup()` stores `currentValue`/`fileHandles`/`ids` directly on `this`, one instance = one set of fields. Supporting "one shared resource, two menu states" means splitting that: keep `folderHandle`/`fileHandles`/`onlineIndex` (what files exist) on the shared object, but move `currentValue`/`ids` (what's selected, which DOM element) into a per-caller sub-record `setup()` returns or keys into.

I'm about halfway through the simpler two-full-instances split already (each mode gets its own `FileFolder.create()`, still reading/writing the same IndexedDB-persisted folder handle). The cost of that approach is just a duplicate folder listing scan per mode-entry — cheap, and self-healing via the existing `refreshFileList()` (already called whenever a dropdown opens).


