That commit already exists — `[REDACTED_SECRET]` on `main` already contains the trapezoid-handle overlap fix, the pitch-label offset, and the null-endIndex phantom-marker fix, so there's nothing new to commit there.

What's uncommitted right now is different, newer work: you challenged my "Random mode has no meaningful start/end" framing ("why wouldn't random have positions? They exist, they just grow the same way Compose does"), and you were right — `state.endIndex` already tracks Random's frontier, and the sliding window itself has real edges. I changed `updateDifficultyUI`'s Random branch to pass the window's own `windowStart`/`windowEnd-1` as real markers (falling back to `null` only when the window is genuinely empty, e.g. at note 0), plus a `Timeline._positionMarker` fallback so the end marker still renders even when there's no "next note" or padding rest to anchor on (Random's window has non-contiguous ids, unlike a full song). Verified red→green with two new tests.

While running the full suite I also caught one unrelated failure — `stopping preview restores the note list to reflect actual game progress` — which turned out to be the same enharmonic-spelling omission (missing `keySignature` arg to `Tonnetz.getNoteName`) that I fixed elsewhere earlier this session but missed in this one test. Fixed and verified green. Full suite is re-running now; I'll commit once it's clean.


