Found the real mechanism, and it connects directly to what you just asked for. A piece can have both in-bounds and off-board cells (now kept). When a line clear removes only the in-bounds portion, `_resplitGroups` correctly splits the survivors — but if the off-board remnant was only connected *through* the now-deleted in-bounds cells, it survives alone with **[REDACTED_SECRET]**, permanently stuck. That's the floating pink piece. Your fix and my bug are the same thing: clearing a line should take the whole row, in or out of the cup.


