### 2026-08-22T17:33:17.634Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

I found the actual "disjointed" cause — and it's unrelated to my fixes. Frame capture only triggers on "cell count changed" ([REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]), but Snake never has a `Board`/`SandboxMode` for `getCellCountSnapshot` to read, so `cellCount` is always `null` for Snake, and it falls back to capturing only every 3 seconds of recorded time. With 507 events over that span, most single-step moves between frames are silently skipped — so consecutive frames genuinely aren't adjacent moves, they're snapshots minutes apart. That's a real, separate, pre-existing gap in the tool (Snake was apparently never plumbed into this capture heuristic), not corruption from the flourish/mode-click fixes.


