- **Plus one larger, calculated `setTimeout`** to resume normal ticking: `notes.length * 100 + 250` ms — i.e., however long the per-cell arpeggio takes, plus a fixed 250ms pause at the end before movement resumes.

So for that 4-long snake, the finish timeout is `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`, and it's a separate, independently-scheduled timer from the four note timeouts — all `N+1` timeouts are set up front, all at once, when the gem is eaten.


### 2026-08-22T18:01:20.681Z | claude (sonnet) | user | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

