### 2026-08-22T18:27:16.495Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Currently, they're **silently dropped**. Confirmed directly in `setupKeyboardEvents` (`[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`):

```js
if (this.state.isGameOver) return;
if (this.state.isPaused || this.state.isFlourishing) return;
// ... direction-key handling below this point
```

Any direction key pressed while `isFlourishing` is true never reaches the direction-mapping code at all — it's not queued, not buffered, just discarded. The player's next keypress *after* the flourish ends is what actually takes effect; anything pressed during the arpeggio itself has no effect whatsoever, not even a "last one wins" queuing.

That's existing, pre-this-conversation behavior, and my planned refactor doesn't change it by default — I'd keep it exactly as-is unless you want it changed (e.g., buffering the last direction pressed during a flourish so it applies the instant movement resumes, rather than requiring the player to notice the flourish ended and press again). Want that left alone, or added as part of this work?


