### 2026-08-22T19:17:35.834Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Committed as `[REDACTED_SECRET]`. Summary of this session's work on Snake's flourish:

**Root regression fixed** (`js/snake.js`): leaving Snake mode mid-flourish and returning used to freeze movement forever — `cleanup()` only marked `isPaused` when a normal move-timer was running (always `null` while flourishing), and separately cancelled the one timeout that would ever clear `isFlourishing`. Reproduced live with real timers before touching anything.

**Redesign**: the flourish went from N independently-scheduled `setTimeout`s (fragile, not resumable, doesn't survive a frozen clock) to a resumable step sequence — `flourishStep` is real state, advanced one at a time by `tick()` itself at a fixed 100ms cadence. Pausing/leaving just clears one pending timeout without losing progress; resuming continues from the same step with fresh timing.

**New behavior, as you asked for**: direction keys and MIDI-note steering now queue during a flourish instead of being silently dropped, and the on-screen keypad brightens whichever direction is currently queued at any time, including mid-flourish.

**Verification**: 10 new Playwright tests (all confirmed red against pre-fix code, green after), full suite (268 Playwright + 38 unit tests) green, plus a real-browser check with actual (non-mocked) timers confirming the whole flow end-to-end. Along the way found and worked around a genuine Playwright/sinon fake-clock precision quirk (not a bug in the app) that caused rare test flakiness at exact 100ms boundaries.

Ready for your next pair of games whenever you'd like — the `reset`/`gameover` markers from earlier plus this fix should make the next recording much more tractable to work with.


