### 2026-08-24T01:46:49.158Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Not just for fun, actually — it's a good idea for real coverage. This codebase has real, documented resize-handling logic (`ResizeObserver`-driven `refreshBoard()` calls, aspect-fit recalculation — [REDACTED_SECRET] in the code comments, with a real past bug: "the mobile drawer's open/close animation leaving the board offset stuck mid-transition"). A session that never resizes never exercises any of that. Deliberately resizing/rotating mid-session would.

One thing to flag though: the *current* story-test convention doesn't actually replay resizes faithfully — Blast/Gravity ignore mid-session resize events entirely, and I did the same for Snake (treated the mid-session portrait→landscape resize as a "liberty," just setting the final settled viewport once up front). So if you record sessions with real resizing in them, I'd need to extend the replay loop to call `page.setViewportSize()` at each recorded `resize` event in sequence, not just at the start — otherwise a resize-heavy session would get recorded but then flattened away when built into a test, same as this one just was, and you wouldn't actually get the coverage. That's a small, contained change to the replay convention, not a blocker — just worth doing deliberately rather than by accident if resize-varying sessions are coming.


