Found four new open issues (#22–25), all filed against very recent code (`[REDACTED_SECRET]`, effectively current — one commit before my last D-pad symmetry fix). Here's what I've found so far:

**#22 "Gravity story" + #23 "Snake story on mobile"** — these are actually **the same continuous recording**: identical seed (`[REDACTED_SECRET]`) and identical start timestamp, so #23's 2679-event file is a superset of #22's 2452-event one (the user kept playing after the first bug report, into Snake, then filed a second one). Neither issue has a written description — #22 has none at all; #23's real complaint is in a follow-up comment: **"Landscape is unplayable — controls are not fully on-screen, everything zoomed in too far."** I checked the attached screenshot and confirmed it visually: the hex board is massively over-zoomed, Snake's six-direction D-pad is entirely missing from view, and only two small stray circular buttons float in the bottom-right corner. Real, confirmed layout bug, landscape-specific. #22 itself I haven't diagnosed yet — no description, would need to actually watch the replay.

**#24 "Sandbox places piece when selecting a new piece type, making it impossible to remove a piece"** — clearly described bug, short 40-event repro attached (different session, different seed). Haven't investigated the code yet.

**#25 "Not all buttons visible at top"** — confirmed visually from the screenshot: the header icon row (mosquito/MIDI/rotate/copy/paste/undo) overflows a narrow viewport with no wrapping, so copy and undo get cut off past the right edge. User confirms they still work when tapped blind, purely a visibility bug.

That's four distinct real bugs across two sessions. Given the scope, how would you like me to prioritize — all four in sequence, or a specific one first?


