### 2026-08-26T16:55:56.465Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Confirmed — yes, exactly that. `⧉` (U+29C9, copy-btn) and `↶` (U+21B6, undo-btn) are obscure Unicode symbols outside the standard emoji block. Most fonts — including this headless Chromium and apparently your real device — have no glyph for them at all, so the browser paints nothing: no tofu box, just blank. The button's box model, padding, and click handler are all completely intact (hence it takes up space and still responds to taps) — only the visible glyph is missing. All the *other* header icons (🦟🎹🔄📋) are real emoji with near-universal font coverage, which is why only these two vanish.

Same two glyphs were also used in the recent [REDACTED_SECRET] (`⧉`/`⎘` for copy/paste, `↶` for undo) — likely the same bug there. I'll fix the header first (issue #25's actual scope) with a regression test, then check Compose.


