### 2026-08-28T06:41:24.273Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

The drawer redesign is done, tested, and committed. Here's where things landed:

**Implemented and verified:**
- Drawer defaults open at every viewport; no more collapsed-on-load.
- Always-visible 32px rail (chevron + mode indicator + action icons) at the true screen edge, same mechanism on desktop and mobile.
- Auto-collapse only on the first real board/D-pad tap on small viewports — not on mode-select.
- Sandbox's palette now uses the same floating-queue overlay as Blast/Gravity; chord guide stays put in the sidebar like Snake/Life.
- `#piece-list` is single-column everywhere.
- Safe-area-top padding + `100dvh` throughout.

**Bugs this surfaced and fixed along the way** (all with regression coverage):
1. The auto-collapse listener was firing on taps inside floating UI (palette, chord-guide reset), reflowing mid-click and silently dropping the interaction — narrowed to an allowlist (board + D-pad only) and deferred so it never disrupts the tap that triggered it.
2. A resize-triggered board redraw (Sandbox/Melody) was wiping an in-progress ghost/highlight since it isn't part of persisted state — now restored.
3. The chord guide's dropdown/reset button was genuinely covered by the floating palette in Sandbox on mobile (not just visually rough) — added clearance.
4. Old story-replay fixtures went nondeterministic because the drawer's one-shot auto-collapse is invisible to recordings made before it existed, and its exact timing races the next replayed tap — `replay-driver.js` now settles once, with real-time waits (rAF hangs under the frozen page-clock stories use for tick catch-up).

**Test status:** `node tests/run_tests.js`, `mobile.spec.js` (162), `invariants.spec.js` (126), `desktop.spec.js` + both `stories.*.spec.js` (285) all green, across every project (Mobile/Tablet Chrome, Mobile Safari, Desktop Chrome).

**One known minor rough edge, not fixed:** at very short landscape heights (~331px, e.g. 817×331), the expanded drawer's mode-tab list needs scrolling to reach every mode — it's reachable (covered by passing tests), just below the fold visually. Flagged in the original plan as a thing to check; didn't rise to blocking.

Everything's committed (`[REDACTED_SECRET]` for the redesign, `[REDACTED_SECRET]` for the new `scripts/screenshot-drawer.js` visual-QA tool). Screenshots are attached above — desktop/portrait/landscape, each expanded and collapsed.


