### 2026-08-28T06:59:52.764Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Fixed all four issues. Here's what was wrong and what changed:

**1. Chord dropdown beside the carousel, wasting space** — and **3. big gap between carousel and chord guide (portrait)** — and **4. carousel only starting halfway across**: these were all one root cause. The palette (carousel) was floating in its own small top-right box (~45% width, matching Blast/Gravity's tiny "next piece" preview), while the chord guide sat separately in normal document flow, so I'd papered over the overlap with a guessed 200px margin — correct for the guide's tallest possible case, wildly excessive most of the time, and still visually disconnected from the carousel. Fixed properly: `#sidebar` itself (already the real parent of both) now becomes one wide floating panel for Sandbox specifically, holding the carousel and chord guide stacked in an ordinary flex column — full width, no gap-guessing, no separate boxes. Blast/Gravity's own small corner queue is untouched.

**2. Landscape screenshot's teal bar + empty space**: a real bug, not just something needing a scroll. `#top-drawer` still had the old portrait-era fixed `height: 60px` from the base rule — I'd changed the landscape drawer's *width* behavior for the collapse animation but never overridden its height, so the whole title+mode-tabs column was clipped to a 60px window instead of the full header height. The mode-slider (280px by design) was real, it just had almost nowhere to render.

**Also removed** the "Chord Guide" heading — the dropdown's own "Choose a Chord" placeholder already says it.

All committed, and verified against the existing test suite (the drawer/chord/palette tests all still pass). The full `npx playwright test` run is going in the background now to repopulate `screenshots/` per your ask — it's a large suite (many spec files × 4 browser projects), so it'll take a while yet. I'll let you know when it's done; you can also check progress yourself with `! tail -20 /[REDACTED_SECRET]` or just watch `screenshots/` fill in.


