### 2026-08-28T07:34:19.888Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Fixed and committed all four issues you flagged:

1. **Chord dropdown beside the carousel / double space**: `#sidebar` itself now becomes one floating panel holding the carousel and chord guide stacked, instead of two separately-positioned things.
2. **Big gap between carousel and chord guide**: was a guessed 200px margin sized for the worst case; replaced with the panel's own natural flex spacing.
3. **Carousel only starting halfway across**: now spans the panel's full width instead of the old ~45%-wide corner box.
4. **Chord Guide label**: removed.

That first pass at the fix was too aggressive though — a 55vh height cap on the combined panel reached the board's vertical center on short viewports and broke real board interaction (piece pickup/placement, panning), caught by the exploratory suite. Capped it at a flat 200px instead, matching Blast/Gravity's own queue precedent, and re-verified against the specific tests that broke — all green now.

Also fixed the actual landscape "teal bar + empty space" bug: `#top-drawer` was still carrying a stale 60px height from the pre-redesign base rule, clipping the whole title+mode-tabs column instead of using the full header height.

Full suite is running again in the background to regenerate `[REDACTED_SECRET]` with all of this in. One heads up: I found a handful of pre-existing Gravity board-fit failures in the random-tap matrix (present before my session too, at different random sizes each run — I haven't touched Gravity's code) — those aren't part of this work, flagging so you don't mistake them for a regression when you review.


