Found it precisely — this isn't a race condition, it's a real bug in the **[REDACTED_SECRET]**. The app computes note names via `Tonnetz.getNoteName(midi, MelodyMode.state.keySignature)` (key-signature-aware), but the test's own expected-value computation calls `Tonnetz.getNoteName(midi)` with no key signature — always assuming sharps. Since Melody's default is a genuinely random unseeded melody each run, whenever the random notes happen to best-fit a flat-leaning key, the app correctly shows a flat name while the test still expects a sharp — a mismatch, not a flake in the traditional sense. Let me fix the test.


