My apologies! That was entirely my fault. 

When my script generated the `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` file, it attempted to join the cell arrays with a newline character, but I accidentally double-escaped the backslash (`\\n` instead of `\n`). 

Because of that, it wrote the literal characters `\n` into the YAML array instead of an actual carriage return. The UI parser choked on the malformed YAML array and just rendered a single dead cell instead of the sprawling collision field!

I just fixed the bug in both the Glider Gun demo and the Eater demo, and patched the extraction script so it won't happen again. 

If you refresh the Tonncade UI, the Turing Glider Gun should now perfectly spawn! You will see the initial glider immediately crash into the block, cause a small localized explosion, and then the core will stabilize and start infinitely firing new gliders outward.


